Note on LLM usage:
LLM based tools may be used to create parts of this project, including code and
documentation. Where this is the case, and a significant part of a Git commit
has been created by or with the assistance of an LLM, this *must* be clearly
indicated using an `Assisted-by` tag at the bottom of the commit message. The
human who creates the commit and submits the code/documentation *must* carefully
review and *fully understand* all the submitted changes. The `Signed-off-by` tag
at the bottom of the commit message is an attestation that the human author has
performed the review, *fully understands* the changes, and agrees that the
changes are meaningful to the project and consistent with the commit message.
